<< /A 35 0 R /Alt (Path diagram showing relationships between adaptive behavior, gross motor, fine motor, language, and personal-social skills with developmental level, which mediates the relationship between serum 25\(OH\)D level and CARS scores. Indirect and total effects are indicated with corresponding coefficients.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Side-by-side diagrams labeled \(a\) and \(b\) show models linking serum 25\(OH\)D level, developmental level, and CARS scores, with developmental level influenced by adaptive behavior, gross motor, fine motor, language, and personal-social skills, including standardized coefficients and significance levels for each path. Indirect and total effects are shown at the bottom for each model.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Grouped horizontal stacked bar charts compare normalized contributions of five predictor variables\204language, personal-social, fine motor, adaptive behavior, and gross motor\204across three models: Random Forest, XGBoost, and LightGBM. Panel \(a\) shows language has the highest normalized contribution while panel \(b\) shows the contributions are more evenly distributed. Each colored segment within bars represents a different model with percentages labeled. Legend indicating model color coding is present. X-axis represents normalized contribution in percent, and y-axis lists predictor variables.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
